<div class="xsto-container py-8 md:py-12 mr-discovery"><script type="application/ld+json">{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Article","headline":"Which XSTO is right for you?","description":"Choose between XSTO M4, M4B, M4 Pro, X12 and X12 Pro with a practical guide to everyday use, seating, transport, demonstrations and pricing.","inLanguage":"en-GB","dateModified":"2026-10-01","mainEntityOfPage":"https://mobilityrobot.co.uk/pages/choosing-an-xsto-wheelchair","author":{"@id":"https://mobilityrobot.co.uk/#organization"},"publisher":{"@id":"https://mobilityrobot.co.uk/#organization"}}</script><p class="mr-discovery-eyebrow">Find your fit</p><header class="mb-8 max-w-3xl"><script type="application/ld+json">{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"BreadcrumbList","itemListElement":[{"@type":"ListItem","position":1,"name":"Home","item":"https://mobilityrobot.co.uk"},{"@type":"ListItem","position":2,"name":"Buyer guides","item":"https://mobilityrobot.co.uk/pages/guides"},{"@type":"ListItem","position":3,"name":"Which XSTO is right for you?","item":"https://mobilityrobot.co.uk/pages/choosing-an-xsto-wheelchair"}]}</script><nav aria-label="Breadcrumb" class="mb-4 text-xs text-muted-foreground"><ol class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2"><li class="flex items-center gap-2"><a href="/" class="hover:text-gold">Home</a></li><li class="flex items-center gap-2"><span aria-hidden="true">/</span><a href="/pages/guides" class="hover:text-gold">Buyer guides</a></li><li class="flex items-center gap-2"><span aria-hidden="true">/</span><span aria-current="page" class="font-medium text-foreground">Which XSTO is right for you?</span></li></ol></nav><h1 class="text-3xl font-bold text-foreground md:text-4xl">Which XSTO is right for you?</h1><p class="mt-3 text-lg text-muted-foreground">Choose between XSTO M4, M4B, M4 Pro, X12 and X12 Pro with a practical guide to everyday use, seating, transport, demonstrations and pricing.</p></header><div class="mr-discovery-article-layout"><article class="mr-discovery-article" aria-label="Which XSTO is right for you?"><p class="mr-discovery-note">Updated <time dateTime="2026-10-01">1 October 2026</time> · Mobility Robot buying guidance</p><p>Start by comparing everyday access, seating, transfers and transport. The M4, M4B and M4 Pro offer everyday self-levelling options, while the X12 and X12 Pro add stair-climbing capability for suitable stairs with assessment and training.</p><section aria-labelledby="everyday-priorities"><h2 id="everyday-priorities">Start with your everyday priorities</h2><p>Write down the things you want your next wheelchair to make easier. They might include getting around at home, going out, sitting at different heights, finding a comfortable position or negotiating a particular route.</p><p>Then consider practical limits: the space in your home, vehicle access, charging arrangements and who will lift or load the chair. These details help narrow your choice.</p></section><section aria-labelledby="m4"><h2 id="m4">M4: everyday self-levelling</h2><p>The XSTO M4 combines self-levelling control with electric seat lifting and a modular design. Compare the folded dimensions and component weights with your transport needs.</p><p>During a demonstration, try the seat-height adjustment and the controls you will use most often. Ask to see how folding and disassembly work in practice.</p><div class="mr-discovery-article-links"><a href="/products/buy-robot-wheelchair">Explore the XSTO M4 <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-arrow-up-right" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M7 7h10v10" /> <path d="M7 17 17 7" /></svg></a></div></section><section aria-labelledby="m4b"><h2 id="m4b">M4B: a practical variation on the M4</h2><p>The XSTO M4B builds on the M4 with an improved folding footrest and new front suspension. If you are choosing between these two models, try their controls, handling and transfer setup side by side.</p><p>Look at the dimensions and total weight as well as the shared technology. Small differences can matter when you are moving through a particular doorway or loading a vehicle.</p><div class="mr-discovery-article-links"><a href="/products/xsto-m4b-1">Explore the XSTO M4B <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-arrow-up-right" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M7 7h10v10" /> <path d="M7 17 17 7" /></svg></a></div></section><section aria-labelledby="m4-pro"><h2 id="m4-pro">M4 Pro: more seating adjustment</h2><p>The M4 Pro offers backrest recline, seat tilt and a different seat-height range. It also has a longer advertised range than the M4. Ask for a seating demonstration and confirm the battery configuration behind the range figure.</p><p>Try the adjustments you would use during a typical day and discuss your existing seating requirements with the team.</p><div class="mr-discovery-article-links"><a href="/products/xsto-m4-pro">Explore the XSTO M4 Pro <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-arrow-up-right" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M7 7h10v10" /> <path d="M7 17 17 7" /></svg></a></div></section><section aria-labelledby="x12"><h2 id="x12">X12: when stair capability matters</h2><p>The X12 adds stair-climbing technology and is a substantially heavier chair. If stairs are central to your decision, start with a suitability assessment. If they are not, compare how an M4-series model matches your everyday requirements.</p><div class="mr-discovery-article-links"><a href="/products/x12-all-terrain-mobility-robot">Explore the XSTO X12 <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-arrow-up-right" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M7 7h10v10" /> <path d="M7 17 17 7" /></svg></a><a href="/pages/stair-climbing-wheelchairs">Read the stair-climbing guide <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-arrow-up-right" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M7 7h10v10" /> <path d="M7 17 17 7" /></svg></a></div></section><section aria-labelledby="cost-and-support"><h2 id="cost-and-support">Compare the full cost and support</h2><p>Check the current chair price, accessories, delivery arrangements and warranty coverage. VAT-relief prices apply only to eligible customers and qualifying purchases; the VAT guide explains the distinction.</p><p>The comparison table brings published figures together. A personal demonstration is the next step towards a decision based on your own requirements.</p><div class="mr-discovery-article-links"><a href="/pages/compare">Compare the models <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-arrow-up-right" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M7 7h10v10" /> <path d="M7 17 17 7" /></svg></a><a href="/pages/vat-relief">Understand VAT relief <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-arrow-up-right" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M7 7h10v10" /> <path d="M7 17 17 7" /></svg></a><a href="/pages/support">Explore delivery and aftercare <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-arrow-up-right" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M7 7h10v10" /> <path d="M7 17 17 7" /></svg></a></div></section><p class="mr-discovery-note">Product information is based on the published XSTO range. Check the relevant product page and confirm current specifications and your chosen configuration with the team before ordering.</p></article><aside class="mr-discovery-sidebar"><nav aria-label="In this guide"><h2>In this guide</h2><ol><li><a href="#everyday-priorities">Start with your everyday priorities</a></li><li><a href="#m4">M4: everyday self-levelling</a></li><li><a href="#m4b">M4B: a practical variation on the M4</a></li><li><a href="#m4-pro">M4 Pro: more seating adjustment</a></li><li><a href="#x12">X12: when stair capability matters</a></li><li><a href="#cost-and-support">Compare the full cost and support</a></li></ol></nav><div class="mr-discovery-aside-cta"><h2>Find your next move.</h2><p>Talk through your requirements with our UK team.</p><a href="/pages/demo" class="mr-discovery-button">Book a demo <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-arrow-up-right" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M7 7h10v10" /> <path d="M7 17 17 7" /></svg></a><a href="/pages/compare" class="mr-discovery-link">Compare models <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-arrow-up-right" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M7 7h10v10" /> <path d="M7 17 17 7" /></svg></a></div></aside></div><section class="mr-discovery-related" aria-labelledby="related-guides-heading"><p class="mr-discovery-eyebrow">Keep exploring</p><h2 id="related-guides-heading">Your next question, answered.</h2><div class="mr-discovery-grid mr-discovery-grid-two"><article class="mr-guide-card"><h3><a href="/pages/self-levelling-wheelchairs">Self-levelling wheelchairs, explained.</a></h3><p>What the technology does, what it does not do, and what to try during a demonstration.</p><a href="/pages/self-levelling-wheelchairs" class="mr-discovery-link">Read the guide <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-arrow-up-right" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M7 7h10v10" /> <path d="M7 17 17 7" /></svg></a></article><article class="mr-guide-card"><h3><a href="/pages/stair-climbing-wheelchairs">Stair-climbing wheelchairs. Start with the right questions.</a></h3><p>The questions to ask about stairs, training and your everyday routes.</p><a href="/pages/stair-climbing-wheelchairs" class="mr-discovery-link">Read the guide <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-arrow-up-right" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M7 7h10v10" /> <path d="M7 17 17 7" /></svg></a></article></div></section></div>
